  "review_notes": [
    "Corrected: יְדֵיהֶם had been marked unrepresented under rule 22 with the note that the ASV renders no word for hands. יָד is not a repeated or resumptive element here, and the ASV's thumbs carries its sense, English writing thumbs of hands only; the pair is now one rule 30 unit headed on בְּהֹנוֹת, matching JDG.1.6.",
    "The competing reading leaves יָד unrepresented; it was rejected on the ground rule 30 gives, that a morpheme whose sense the single English word carries is not left standing beside a neighbour holding the whole rendering.",
    "Threescore and ten is kept whole with the single numeral שִׁבְעִים under rule 42's closing sentence, headed on Threescore.",
    "הָיוּ מְלַקְּטִים is fused on the one word gathered; the competing reading marks the auxiliary unrepresented and is named in that unit's note.",
    "great toes is given whole to רַגְלֵיהֶם, whose own בֹּהֶן the Hebrew gaps, headed on toes.",
    "Partition after correction: all 33 source and 42 target IDs are used exactly once, in 31 units."
